# [[.DisplayName]]

Multi-stack workspace generated by [vibeit](https://github.com/lt-sureshmopidevi/vibeit).

## Open

```bash
cursor [[.Name]]/[[.Name]].code-workspace
```

Each of `backend/`, `web/`, and `app/` is its **own git repository**.

## Quick start (root Makefile)

From this folder:

```bash
make help      # all commands (backend.*, web.*, app.*)
make status    # which stacks exist
make setup     # one-time setup for present stacks
make dev       # backend (bg) + web dev server
make app.run   # Flutter — run in its own terminal
```

Missing stacks are skipped automatically. Add more with `vibeit add`.

## Stacks

| Stack | Path | First run |
|-------|------|-----------|
| Backend (Go + Gin) | `backend/` | `make backend.setup && make backend.run` |
| Web (React + Tailwind) | `web/` | `make web.install && make web.dev` |
| App (Flutter) | `app/` | `make app.get && make app.run` |

Only folders that exist were generated. Add more later:

```bash
vibeit add
```

## Full-stack features

Use `.cursor/skills/add-feature-fullstack` so agents implement **backend → web → app** sequentially (never in parallel for the same feature).

## Agent guardrails

Each stack ships `.cursor/rules` and `.cursor/skills` (architecture, Karpathy guidelines, add-feature with `learned/` auto-log). See each stack’s `AGENTS.md`.
